# Environment variables

Copy to `.env` and fill in only what you need. The app runs fully in the browser
with local storage when Supabase is left unset.

```sh
# --- Supabase (optional) --------------------------------------------------
# Create a project at https://supabase.com, run supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql,
# enable anonymous sign-ins (Auth -> Providers -> Anonymous), then copy the values
# from Project Settings -> API.
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
```

Notes:

- `PUBLIC_`-prefixed variables are exposed to the browser. Do not put a service-role
  key here.
- A Deepgram BYOK key is entered by the user inside the app (Settings), not here.
  It is never added to `.env`.
